  THE HEADLINE GATE IS AGAIN A NEGATIVE ONE: NOTHING PUBLISHED MOVES.
     Every figure on every section page should read exactly as it does
     today, to the digit. This wave changes what the editor accepts, what
     a template marks, and who a write is attributed to. A changed
     published number is a regression, not a fix.
  
  THE ATTRIBUTION, ON ITS EXACT GESTURE. Open Report Data, B2, on a
     scratch year holding 50/10/0/60 and 97/40/0/137. Change Non-DAC L2
     Plugs from 97 to 100 and leave the cell. Total Plugs recomputes to
     140, as before. Press Save Changes: the dialog must say ONE cell
     change, not two, and the change history must record the L2 Plugs
     cell alone. Before this it said two and named Total Plugs 137 to 140
     as an edit under your own name.
     AND THE COUNT MUST NOT UNDER-REPORT: change two cells a person can
     type into and the dialog must say two.
  
  THE G PERCENTAGES ON BLUR. Open G1 on a scratch year, type 500 into a
     category row and leave the cell WITHOUT saving. Read the percentages
     in the draft: they must read as they do after a save, not half of
     it. Before this the blur recompute used a doubled denominator and
     showed 49.33 / 1.34 / 50.67 where load and save both showed 97.36 /
     2.64 / 100.00.
     THE IMPORT PATH WAS NEVER WRONG and must stay right: import a filled
     template into G1 and the imported draft must still read exactly.
  
  THE WORKBOOK MARKER ON A POPULATED YEAR. Download G3s template for a
     year that already holds data and for a fresh one. Both must mark the
     empty total cells (calculated). Before this the populated year read
     County Total and (no value) while the fresh one read (calculated).
     J8 MUST STAY fill-in on both, because those figures belong to the
     preparer and the engine cannot derive them.
  
